%% Storage account network rules - the order in which one request is actually decided - Contoso profile
%% Source: codex/blueprint-azure-files-secure-storage-account.md and codex/playbook-harden-existing-storage-account.md, verified on Microsoft Learn (Azure Storage firewall rules and network access; Guidelines and limitations for the storage firewall; Trusted Azure services for Azure Storage network security)
flowchart TB
  REQ["Request for stmryfiles01 - SMB 445 or FileREST 443"]
  PLANE{"Control plane or data plane"}
  CP["Control plane at management.azure.com - firewall rules do NOT apply here - only Azure RBAC and the CanNotDelete lock do"]
  DP["Data plane at stmryfiles01.file.core.windows.net - network rules are enforced on all protocols, REST and SMB alike"]
  PE{"Arrived on the file private endpoint in the spoke"}
  PEOK["ALLOW - Contoso servers and workstations over ExpressRoute private peering - the public endpoint rule set is never consulted"]
  PNA{"publicNetworkAccess"}
  DIS["Disabled - shuts the public endpoint and takes precedence over defaultAction - never set on a File Sync account, this is runbook class 2"]
  TS{"Caller is a trusted Azure service and bypass includes AzureServices"}
  TSOK["ALLOW - trusted service access takes the highest precedence over every other network restriction - Microsoft.StorageSync change enumeration and Azure Backup jobs ride this leg"]
  RI{"Caller matches a resourceAccessRule"}
  RIOK["ALLOW - resource instance rule pinned to the Storage Sync Service resource id plus the tenant id - same tenant only - the instance own RBAC then decides what it may do"]
  VN{"Source subnet has a Microsoft.Storage service endpoint and a matching virtualNetworkRule"}
  VNOK["ALLOW - up to 400 VNet rules - Microsoft.Storage reaches the same region, Microsoft.Storage.Global any region, only one endpoint type per subnet"]
  IP{"Source public IPv4 matches an ipRule"}
  IPOK["ALLOW - up to 400 IP rules - Contoso baseline lists admin egress addresses only"]
  IPLIM["An IP rule cannot help this caller - RFC1918 ranges are rejected, /31 and /32 prefixes are unsupported, IPv4 only, and an IP rule has no effect on a caller inside the same Azure region"]
  DEF{"networkAcls.defaultAction"}
  DENY["DENY 403 - Contoso target state for everything not matched above"]
  ALLOWSTATE["Allow - the pre-hardening state the assessor reports as SEC-03"]
  AUTHZ["A network pass is not access - the request still faces Kerberos AD DS plus share-level RBAC plus NTFS ACLs, or the account key while allowSharedKeyAccess stays true"]
  REQ --> PLANE
  PLANE -->|ARM operation such as File Shares Delete| CP
  PLANE -->|share and file IO| DP
  DP --> PE
  PE -->|yes| PEOK
  PE -->|no, public endpoint| PNA
  PNA -->|Disabled| DIS
  PNA -->|Enabled| TS
  TS -->|yes| TSOK
  TS -->|no| RI
  RI -->|yes| RIOK
  RI -->|no| VN
  VN -->|yes| VNOK
  VN -->|no| IP
  IP -->|yes| IPOK
  IP -->|no| IPLIM
  IPLIM --> DEF
  DEF -->|Deny| DENY
  DEF -->|Allow| ALLOWSTATE
  PEOK --> AUTHZ
  TSOK --> AUTHZ
  RIOK --> AUTHZ
  VNOK --> AUTHZ
  IPOK --> AUTHZ
  ALLOWSTATE --> AUTHZ
